SUMMARY:[Neuromorphic & Brain-inspired Computing][Computational Neuroscienc
 e] NICE 2027 - Regular research paper submission deadline
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: Neuro Inspired Computational Elements Confere
 nce\nWebsite: https://niceworkshop.org/nice-2027/\nSource URL: https://ea
 sychair.org/cfp/nice2027\nLocation: Brighton\, United Kingdom\nTopics: Ne
 uromorphic & Brain-inspired Computing\, Computational Neuroscience\, Mach
 ine Learning\, BCI & Neurotechnology\nSize: M\nSubmission type: Research 
 papers + late-breaking abstracts\nConfidence: confirmed\nLast checked dat
 e: 2026-10-08\nNotes: Main conference April 6-8\; dedicated tutorials Apr
 il 9. Accepted proceedings research papers are published through IEEE\; l
 ate-breaking abstracts are non-archival\, and some poster contributions m
 ay not enter the proceedings. Neither a scheduled opening nor a live subm
 ission portal has been verified. Size is an editorial estimate.\nScope: N
 euromorphic and brain-inspired computing at the intersection of neuroscie
 nce\, algorithms and hardware. Characteristic work includes spiking neura
 l networks\, learning in neural systems\, event-driven computation\, neur
 omorphic processors and embodied applications. Research papers and late-b
 reaking abstracts are different contribution routes.\nAdditional topics: 
